  "public": {
    "bounded_reading": "Cook 2013 abstract ratings, its author self-ratings, Doran and Zimmerman 2009 survey responses, and Cook 2016's synthesis range are related evidence, but they do not measure one identical population and quantity.",
    "practical_reading": "When citing a percentage, name the study, denominator, population or document set, question or coding rule, and whether the figure covers only records that expressed a position.",
    "slug": "what-the-97-percent-climate-consensus-studies-measure",
    "title": "What the 97% climate-consensus studies measure",
    "why_it_matters": "The familiar 97% shorthand can blur materially different populations and measured quantities."
  },
